.TH PLAYLIST-CHECKER 1 "October 2026" "playlist-checker 1.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
playlist-checker \- check IPTV and internet radio playlists for dead streams and duplicates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playlist-checker
.RI [ PLAYLIST | URL | LIST.txt ]...
.br
.B playlist-checker
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B playlist-checker
is a desktop application that opens TV (IPTV) and internet radio playlists in
M3U, M3U8, PLS and XSPF format (also gzip-compressed .m3u.gz, .m3u8.gz,
.pls.gz and .xspf.gz), from files, whole folders (including subfolders) or web
addresses, and checks every stream.
.PP
It recognises HTTP and HTTPS streams, HLS (it tests the real video segment),
Icecast and Shoutcast radio, and RTMP, RTSP and MMS servers. Per-channel
User-Agent and Referer settings (#EXTVLCOPT, or url|User-Agent=...) are used
when checking.
.PP
Duplicates (same stream address, optionally same channel name) are marked.
Groups can be included, excluded, renamed, merged and reordered. A new clean
playlist can be saved, keeping channel logos, EPG information (tvg-id,
url-tvg) and player options, optionally as one file per group. A CSV report of
the check can be exported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PLAYLIST
Playlist files to open at start.
.TP
.I URL
Web addresses (http:// or https://) of playlists to download at start.
.TP
.I LIST.txt
A text file with one playlist address per line. Every playlist is downloaded
(four at a time) and its channels are added; see LISTS OF PLAYLIST ADDRESSES.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH LISTS OF PLAYLIST ADDRESSES
File \(-> Open list of playlist URLs (Ctrl+L) reads a .txt file with one
address per line. Empty lines and lines starting with #, ; or // are ignored,
and text before an address is allowed. Addresses that return a single stream
are added as one channel, local playlist files are opened, and addresses that
fail are listed at the end. Stop cancels the remaining downloads. With
Settings \(-> Check new channels automatically after loading, the new channels
are checked as soon as they are loaded. An example list is installed in
.IR /usr/share/doc/playlist-checker/examples/ .
.SH GEO-BLOCKED CHANNELS
Channels that work but only show "not available in your country" get the
status Geo-blocked and are left out of the saved playlist. They are found by
the server's answer (HTTP 451, a 403 or web page mentioning your country or
region, a redirect to a "geoblock" address), by a short looping video
instead of a live stream, and \(em when
.BR ffmpeg (1)
is installed \(em by a fingerprint (shape, brightness and colours) of the
picture of each channel. Up to three frames, about 0.8 seconds apart, are
taken: a picture that moves is live TV and never a banner, and a black fade-in
frame is skipped. When several different channels show exactly the same still
picture, and it is still the same a few seconds later, the program shows it
and asks. Versions of one channel
(HD, HEVC, 4K, subtitles, a second source) count as one channel, and a picture
that changes is live TV, not a banner. Right-click a channel showing such a banner and choose "Mark as
geo-blocked": the picture is remembered and recognised on all channels in
this and later checks. The options are in Settings \(-> Detect geo-blocked
channels; Check \(-> Find "not available" banners runs the picture check on
the online channels only.
.SH PLAYLIST COLORS
Every playlist gets its own color: a colored square at the start of each
channel row and, unless switched off in Settings \(-> Tint rows with the
playlist color, a light tint of the row. The Playlists list on the left shows
the colors with the number of channels; click a playlist to show only its
channels, or its \(OK box to leave it out. Unticked groups and playlists are
hidden from the channel list (Settings \(-> Hide unticked groups and playlists
in the channel list), skipped by Check streams and Recheck offline, and left
out of the saved playlist.
With Settings \(-> Remember ticked / unticked groups and playlists (on by
default) unticked groups (by name) and playlists stay unticked the next time
they are opened; Settings \(-> Forget remembered groups and playlists clears
this.
.SH PLAYING CHANNELS
Click the stream address (shown as \(rh) of a channel, double-click the
channel, press Enter, or right-click \(-> Play to watch it. Settings \(-> Video
player chooses the player: Automatic (the first installed of VLC, mpv,
Celluloid, SMPlayer, GNOME Videos and ffplay), one of these, the system's
default application for playlists, or a custom command with the placeholders
{url}, {name}, {ua} and {referer}. The channel's User-Agent and Referer are
passed to VLC, mpv, Celluloid and ffplay. By default the previous player is
closed when another channel is played.
.SH USER-AGENT
Some IPTV providers only answer certain players. Settings \(-> User-Agent lets
the program identify itself as VLC, FFmpeg, mpv, Kodi, ExoPlayer, TiviMate,
IPTV Smarters, a Samsung or LG smart TV, an Enigma2 receiver, a web browser
and others, or as any custom text. A User-Agent set inside the playlist for a
channel (#EXTVLCOPT:http-user-agent or url|User-Agent=...) always wins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/playlist-checker/settings.json
User settings (check timeout, User-Agent, duplicate rules, Settings menu options).
.SH TEMPORARY ERRORS
Servers sometimes fail for a moment (timeout, HTTP 502, 503 or 504 "Gateway
Timeout", connection reset). With Settings \(-> Try again channels with
temporary errors (on by default) such channels are checked once more at the
end of the check, a few seconds later, fewer at once and with twice the time
limit; the check result then says "on the 2nd try" or "(2 tries)". Permanent
errors such as 404 or "server not found" are not tried again.
.SH NOTES
UDP and multicast links can only be tested inside the provider's own network
and are reported as "not checked".
.PP
Channels are played by clicking their stream address (see PLAYING CHANNELS).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/antoxa78/PyPlaylist-Checker
